          "Security posture is good at the top end: none of the 5 known advisories affect the latest version; the single advisory touching ^4.19.2 is resolved by raising the floor within your existing range.",
          "Practical footprint is light: 73 KB unpacked with 28 direct dependencies, and the huge ecosystem means answers and middleware exist for nearly everything.",
          "Two caveats to plan around: it ships no bundled type information (add @types/express for TypeScript), and Express 5 is now the latest line, so a 4.x pin is legacy-adjacent even though 4.x remains fully supported."
